 On an empty table, `related()` has no candidates, so no float is ever written and the first publish succeeds. Once one story exists, the score is computed, `similar` holds a float, and boto3's `put_item` rejects it with the `TypeError` in `logs/error.log`. The existing test only published into an empty table, so it never reached that path.\n\n**Fix:**\n- `src/app.py`: a new `to_dynamo()` converts every float in the item to `Decimal(str(value))` before `put_item`. It covers any float on any path, not just `score`.\n- `tests/test_publish.py`: the write-path tests seed one story first. A new test publishes twice through `handler()` and expects a 201.\n\n**Verification:** all 4 tests pass with the fix. With the original `app.py` restored, the populated-table tests fail with the same `TypeError` as the log.\n\n**Colleague's note:** I used the diagnosis and the seeding approach. I did not switch scores to integer percentages, because that changes what `score` means in stored data. I also did not treat a one-line change as the whole fix, since the boundary conversion covers the other float paths the note warns about.\n\n**Caveat:** values read back from DynamoDB are `Decimal`, which `json.dumps` cannot serialize. The repo has no reader code, so nothing breaks here. If the reader page serializes `score` with `json.dumps`, it needs a conversion on read.\n\nNothing was deployed, published or sent to any external service.","ttft_ms":2000,"type":"result","duration_ms":41277,"uuid":"b57cbcba-8db2-413f-8373-eff6676d121a","ttft_stream_ms":1815,"time_to_request_ms":534,"first_content_frame_ms":1816,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":7229,"cacheReadInputTokens":208566,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16411,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.008983960000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1782,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":16411,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T22:27:53.640Z"}
